set.body:
Route multiset and direct-sum studies through Op, secondOrder, compress, FunctionalFrame, and OperatorProgram.

Scope:
- X_oplus and block row relations remain block/matrix-free;
- every block S_st is constructed by secondOrder(X_s, L_st, X_t);
- multiset association and agreement builders compile to closed core objectives and normalization constraints;
- BlockDesign remains distinct from row relationships;
- partial, weighted, one-to-many, and hub-factorized alignment remain encoded entirely in typed row maps/relations.

Do not generalize the full variational term hierarchy here. Only the finite objective and normalization forms required by current multiset behavior belong to the core; penalties, target expressions, feasible sets, and general lowering belong to the separate variational epic.

Acceptance:
- current DirectSumStudy and multiset suites pass on JVM and JS;
- direct block-matrix oracle and pairwise-versus-direct-sum metamorphic tests agree;
- alignment factorization and row permutation laws pass;
- no dense block assembly;
- result symmetry and component-space compatibility are explicit.
